    "body": "But for this, Firefox outputs 1, which means that `replace(\"a\", \"a\")` does run the update steps if \"a\" is in the token list, even though it's a no-op: https://jsfiddle.net/4d8ja9yw/2/  What does WebKit do?  (I'm still trying to compile WebKit myself, but I can't find non-ancient binaries for Linux, so until I succeed I can't test it.)",
